// 03 · Selection — a priced trait decays when it is not used (with its own control).
//
// Natural selection made legible (SIM Law 7 — every characteristic is priced), and its
// null shown IN THE SAME ARENA — fast enough to WATCH: the advantage is plain inside two
// minutes. One open arena, no barrier: the SAME far-sighted WANDERERS (vision range 300, 21
// rays) forage a dense flora carpet on volcanic vents. A wanderer drifts at random and eats
// what it blunders into — it never STEERS on its eyes — so their vision is pure overhead: a
// heavy metabolic cost (range × rays, `Vision::metabolic_cost` ≈ 3/s at the founding value,
// the dominant drain) that buys nothing.
//   • MUTABLE eyes (species 0) — vision may drift. Because the flora is grazed to a limiting
//     level, a wanderer that spends less on eyes it never uses breeds faster, so selection
//     MELTS the eyes down FAST: within ~2 min the lineage's mean `vision_range` slides from
//     300 to ~210 (and its ray count is pruned too), and — paying far less overhead — it
//     out-breeds the control roughly two-to-three-fold.
//   • FROZEN eyes (species 1) — the CONTROL. Everything drifts exactly as for the mutable
//     species, but its two vision genes are non-mutable, so they cannot move — this lineage
//     stays far-sighted at 300 / 21, keeps paying, and dwindles. Same economy, same drift on
//     every OTHER gene.
//
// Both lineages are founded INTERMIXED (40 each) in the centre of one open arena and forage
// the same vents together — no wall, no side, no rule between them; they compete for one
// shared food base. The founding cohort is deliberately LARGE so the outcome is selection,
// not a coin-flip: with dozens of each lineage the cheaper mutant reliably wins every seed,
// where a handful would let drift decide. The frozen control persists as a shrinking
// minority (the flat 300 line still there to read against). The contrast IS the proof: a
// gene falling only in the species where it is allowed to mutate is selection, not decay
// from noise or crowding. This folds the retired 01_drift's pure baseline in as a live control.
// Give these same eyes to a Hunter that USES them (04) and they are kept — the deliberate
// 03→04 pair. Living food, so the run is an example to watch: the flora oscillates hard
// (Lotka-Volterra, ROADMAP §7) and eventually winds down, long after the decay is plain.
//
// The gene-drift graph is filtered to the two vision genes (`gene_display`) and split by the
// shared species selector (`species_display`): the mutable lineage's eyes melt down (its
// curves slide) right beside the frozen control holding flat — the proof, in one frame. The
// same selector focuses the population graph, where the cheaper mutable lineage pulls ahead.
// Toggle genes from the chips over the drift plot, species from the shared "Species" row.
(
    tick_hz: 64.0,
    arena_half_extent: 400.0,
    archetypes: [
        (
            // Mutable eyes — vision drifts; selection prunes it. Founded intermixed at centre.
            name: "Mutable eyes",
            color: (1.0, 0.5, 0.4),
            count: 40,
            radius: 8.0,
            reserve_max: 120.0,
            genotype: (
                max_speed: 55.0,
                agility: 0.12,
                vision_range: 300.0,
                vision_fov_deg: 120.0,
                reproduction_threshold: 38.0,
                offspring_energy: 19.0,
                mutation_rate: 0.30,
                vision_rays: 21.0,
            ),
            brain: Wander(turn_rate: 0.25),
            mutable: (
                mutation_rate: false,
            ),
            // Both fauna share one central spawn disc → the two lineages start intermixed
            // (radius reaches the inner vents, so founders are near food from tick 0).
            spawn_zone: Some((shape: Circle(center: (0.0, 0.0), radius: 180.0))),
        ),
        (
            // Frozen eyes — the control: same everything, but vision cannot mutate, so it
            // stays put. Founded intermixed at centre.
            name: "Frozen eyes",
            color: (0.3, 0.7, 0.95),
            count: 40,
            radius: 8.0,
            reserve_max: 120.0,
            genotype: (
                max_speed: 55.0,
                agility: 0.12,
                vision_range: 300.0,
                vision_fov_deg: 120.0,
                reproduction_threshold: 38.0,
                offspring_energy: 19.0,
                mutation_rate: 0.30,
                vision_rays: 21.0,
            ),
            brain: Wander(turn_rate: 0.25),
            mutable: (
                mutation_rate: false,
                vision_range: false,
                vision_rays: false,
            ),
            spawn_zone: Some((shape: Circle(center: (0.0, 0.0), radius: 180.0))),
        ),
        (
            // Flora — the shared food base, scattered across the whole arena.
            name: "Flora",
            color: (0.4, 0.85, 0.4),
            count: 200,
            radius: 6.0,
            reserve_max: 50.0,
            genotype: (
                max_speed: 0.0,
                vision_range: 30.0,
                vision_rays: 1.0,
                reproduction_threshold: 18.0,
                offspring_energy: 11.0,
                mutation_rate: 0.0,
                photosynthesis: 7.0,
                seed_dispersal: 20.0,
            ),
            brain: Sessile,
            mutable: (
                max_speed: false,
                agility: false,
                vision_range: false,
                vision_fov: false,
                reproduction_threshold: false,
                offspring_energy: false,
                mutation_rate: false,
                vision_rays: false,
                photosynthesis: false,
                seed_dispersal: false,
                brain_cost: false,
                act_cost: false,
            ),
        ),
    ],
    // A low floor so the useless eyes have room to slide all the way down.
    vision_range_bounds: (min: 30.0, max: 320.0),
    // A gentle cost law: a low metabolic floor lets a clumsy random forager survive between
    // meals, so each lineage sustains a breeding population and selection has generations to
    // act.
    cost_law: (size_exponent: 2.0, maintenance: 0.02, locomotion: 0.012, maneuver: 0.0002, metabolic_cost: 0.25),
    predation: (size_margin: 0.1, range: 8.0, rate: 15.0),
    field_resolution: 256,
    components: [
        (name: "Nutrient", diffusion: 0.3, decay: 0.0, initial: 0.1),
    ],
    // Foreground the two vision genes: their slide is the whole point, and against the
    // other genes' drift it would be easy to miss. Empty would show every mutable gene;
    // the graph's chips toggle this live and the recorded video honors the same choice.
    gene_display: ["Vision range", "Rays (precision)"],
    // The single SPECIES SELECTOR, shared by both graphs. Focus them on the two lineages:
    //   • population graph → the mutable line pulling ahead of the frozen control (food line
    //     and any other species hidden);
    //   • gene-drift graph → split per lineage, each gene keeping its own color, so the
    //     mutable eyes MELTING read beside the frozen control HOLDING flat (same hue, one
    //     sliding, one flat) — the contrast the pooled mean hid; the legend names the lineage.
    // Clear it (deselect both from the "Species" chips) to fall back to all species / pooled.
    species_display: ["Mutable eyes", "Frozen eyes"],
    sources: [
        // Ten vents in two symmetric clusters flanking the central spawn — one shared food
        // base both intermixed lineages forage. Dense enough to reach the food-limited
        // regime (where the vision cost bites) yet sustain both through the window. Upper-left:
        (pos: (-250.0, 150.0), component: 0, rate: 20.0, color: (1.0, 0.55, 0.2), radius: 12.0),
        (pos: (-150.0, 250.0), component: 0, rate: 20.0, color: (1.0, 0.55, 0.2), radius: 12.0),
        (pos: (-100.0, 120.0), component: 0, rate: 20.0, color: (1.0, 0.55, 0.2), radius: 12.0),
        (pos: (-220.0, 40.0), component: 0, rate: 20.0, color: (1.0, 0.55, 0.2), radius: 12.0),
        (pos: (-60.0, 300.0), component: 0, rate: 20.0, color: (1.0, 0.55, 0.2), radius: 12.0),
        // Lower-right:
        (pos: (250.0, -150.0), component: 0, rate: 20.0, color: (1.0, 0.55, 0.2), radius: 12.0),
        (pos: (150.0, -250.0), component: 0, rate: 20.0, color: (1.0, 0.55, 0.2), radius: 12.0),
        (pos: (100.0, -120.0), component: 0, rate: 20.0, color: (1.0, 0.55, 0.2), radius: 12.0),
        (pos: (220.0, -40.0), component: 0, rate: 20.0, color: (1.0, 0.55, 0.2), radius: 12.0),
        (pos: (60.0, -300.0), component: 0, rate: 20.0, color: (1.0, 0.55, 0.2), radius: 12.0),
    ],
    field_relations: [
        // Both wanderers: need the nutrient (flora digestible), hold it, breed on it — the
        // identical economy; only vision's mutability differs between the two.
        (species: 0, component: 0, capacity: 30.0, emit_at_death: 3.0, repro_cost: 12.0, need: 1.0),
        (species: 1, component: 0, capacity: 30.0, emit_at_death: 3.0, repro_cost: 12.0, need: 1.0),
        // Flora: absorbs & holds the nutrient, seeds on it, recycles at death.
        (species: 2, component: 0, absorb: 2.5, capacity: 10.0, emit_at_death: 5.0),
    ],
    random_initial_nutrients: true,
    seed: 1,
)
